---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Section from "@/components/Section.astro";
import Container from "@/components/Container.astro";
import SectionHeading from "@/components/SectionHeading.astro";
import DecorativeImage from "@/components/DecorativeImage.astro";
import HamaynkSite from '@/assets/images/hamaynk-site.jpg';
import HamaynkGroup from '@/assets/images/hamaynk-group-photo.png';
import HamaynkGroupWork from '@/assets/images/hamaynk-group-work.png';
import Arin from '@/assets/images/arin.gif';

// Page metadata
const title = "About";
const description = "About Hamaynk, a website for Armenian events in New England";
const seoTitle = "About";
const seoDescription = "About Hamaynk, a website for Armenian events in New England";
---

<Layout {title} {description} {seoTitle} {seoDescription}>
	<Section>
		<Container>
			<SectionHeading>
				<h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-wide font-caveat-brush">About Us</h1>
				<DecorativeImage src={HamaynkGroup} alt="Hamaynk Group Photo" variant="card" />
				<p>Hamaynk was founded in 2026 by the inaugural cohort of NAASR’s NextGen Summer Program developed and taught by Dr. Lisa Gulesserian:
				</p>
				<p>Siran Arakelian, Edmon Arzunyan, Mané Arzunyan, Vanessa Atakian, Meliné Demirjian, John Esserian, Aleks Hovhannisyan, Narineh Mardiros, Patil Mardiros, and David Oganesian.</p>
			</SectionHeading>
		</Container>
	</Section>

	<Section class:list={"bg-neutral-50"}>
		<Container>
			<SectionHeading>
				<h2 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-wide">Our Story</h2>
				<DecorativeImage src={HamaynkSite} alt="Hamaynk Website" variant="card" />
				<p>
				As part of the Armenian youth, we have been dissatisfied by existing methods for finding appealing local events as well as the limited number of such opportunities. Our frustration was attested by the findings of the <a href="https://www.armeniandiasporasurvey.com" target="_blank" class="text-blue-500 underline">Armenian Diaspora Survey</a> which stated that 37% of survey respondents “claimed lack of events interesting to the youth.”
				</p>
				<p>
				With Hamaynk, we seek to collect, curate, and categorize Armenian events in New England and filter them by your interests, age group, and more. Additionally, we provide ideas and resources to encourage Armenians in our community to host their own events.
				</p>
			</SectionHeading>
		</Container>
	</Section>

	<Section>
		<Container>
			<SectionHeading>
				<h2 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-wide">Name & Mascot</h2>
				<p>We chose the name Hamaynk because it means “community” in Armenian. Through this website, we strive to connect Armenian youth in New England.
				</p>
				<DecorativeImage src={Arin} alt="Mascot Arin winking" variant="card" isGif={true} />
				<p>
				Our mascot Arin (Արին) is a welcome swallow (ծիծեռնակ), which is a notable animal in Armenian culture that represents hope and renewal.</p>
			</SectionHeading>
		</Container>
	</Section>


	<Section class:list={"bg-neutral-50"}>
		<Container class:list={"lg:py-12"}>
			<SectionHeading>
				<h2 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-wide">Future Plans</h2>
				<DecorativeImage src={HamaynkGroupWork} alt="Hamaynk Group Work" variant="card" />
				<p>
				We plan to expand Hamanyk to the rest of the United States so that we can connect more Armenians in the diaspora. Additionally, we hope to create a user-friendly app version of Hamanyk, with user notifications and an automated approval system.
				</p>
			</SectionHeading>
		</Container>
	</Section>

</Layout>
